.TH PZSTD 1 "September 2026" "Zstandard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pzstd \- parallel Zstandard compressor and decompressor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pzstd
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pzstd
compresses and decompresses data in the Zstandard format using multiple
worker threads.  During compression it splits input into independently
compressed frames and concatenates them into a standards-compliant stream.
It accepts the same core command-line interface as
.BR zstd (1),
with an additional option for selecting the worker count.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p " threads"
.TQ
.BI \-\-processes " threads"
Use the specified number of worker threads.
.TP
.BR \-d , " \-\-decompress"
Decompress input.
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Write output to
.IR file .
.TP
.BR \-c , " \-\-stdout"
Write output to standard output.
.TP
.BR \-f , " \-\-force"
Overwrite output without prompting and process symbolic links.
.TP
.BR \-k , " \-\-keep"
Preserve input files.  This is the default.
.TP
.BR \-t , " \-\-test"
Test compressed-file integrity without writing decompressed output.
.TP
.BI \- "#"
Select compression level 1 through 19.  The default is 3.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Display the complete option summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Display version information and exit.
.SH NOTES
Dictionary mode is not supported by
.BR pzstd .
Streams produced by it can be decompressed by any conforming Zstandard
implementation.  Parallel decompression is available for streams produced by
.BR pzstd ;
ordinary Zstandard streams are read and decompressed through separate threads.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zstd (1)
